 "channel_basis": "Macro LEF: 144 M4 signal pins on each of the left and right edges, all in the y band 0.768-14.496 um (0.096 um pitch); M1-M4 OBS over the macro; M5+ free. Pins exist on both vertical edges, so no orientation makes every pin face the core. Outer channel need: one vertical M5 escape track (0.048 um pitch) per outer pin = 144 tracks; after the 2 um halo and the ~14% M5 PG share (0.12 um straps + 0.072 spacing per net at 2.7 um), a 10.8 um channel gives (10.8-2)/0.048*0.86 = 157 >= 144. The 5.4 um baseline gives 61. Core-side: inner pins escape on M4 straight into the 249.48 um logic region; the macro stack is centred vertically so both pin bands (bottom of rom0 R0/MY, top of rom1 MX/R180) abut free std-cell rows on their outer-y side as well. rom0/rom1 are 64.8 um apart (the next 2.16 um joint site/M4 grid point above 62.91), so the macros never overlap.",
